  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved labour administration, social protection, wages systems and workplace compliance policies in the Cook Islands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Cook Islands has prioritsed the improvement of labour administration and social protection as two key areas for development in this biennium. The ILO continues to support the strengthening and implementation of social protection systems to safeguard workers&apos; rights and well-being. This includes initiatives aimed at improving access to healthcare, maternity protection, unemployment benefits, and other social services. In this regard, the ILO also provides technical support to ensure adequate social protection measures are in place through the review of the Employment Relations Act 2012 as well as the Workplace Health and Safety Act compliance. 

The ILO is also supporting the Cook Islands on the development of the National Minimum Wage Policy working with local stakeholders to establish fair and sustainable wage systems. This involves regular reviews and adjustments of minimum wage rates to reflect economic conditions such as inflation and cost of living. Through these efforts, the ILO aims to foster a more equitable and sustainable labour market in the Cook Islands, ensuring decent work and improved living standards for all its citizens.</narrative>
  </description>
